# Project: Fake News Detection System

This is my **flagship portfolio project** — the most important one for landing a forward deployment / backend infrastructure role. Treat it with that weight.

---

# Origin & Purpose

- Originated from a college seminar project on fake news detection using NLP
- Evolved into the centerpiece of my AI backend portfolio
- Goal: demonstrate I can build production-grade AI infrastructure in Go, not just wrap APIs

---

# Architecture Overview

```
Client Request
     ↓
[Go API Gateway]          ← main entry point, routing, auth, rate limiting
     ↓
[Stage 1: DeBERTa-v3-small classifier]
     ↓
  confidence ≥ 85%? ──YES──→ return result
     ↓ NO
[Stage 2: LLM + RAG fallback]
     ├── Qdrant vector DB  ← semantic search over knowledge base
     └── LLM reasoning     ← context-augmented classification
     ↓
  return result
```

**Key components:**
- Go API Gateway — the part I own most deeply
- Two-stage ML pipeline — Python services behind the gateway
- Qdrant — vector database for RAG retrieval
- 85% confidence threshold triggers the fallback

